#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Record and cut a calm vertical film of the land: a walk through its kinds
of country, from the coast up to the high fells and into the night.

  tools/vista OUTPUT.mp4 [--work DIR] [--fresh] [--draft] [--only CLIP..]

Like tools/trailer, the game records every clip itself (tools/record), so
the film is the same on any machine.  Most of it is held drone views of the
default world (seed 123, 2048 samples, play), composed as shot lists like
data/opening.txt and recorded in one reel per hour of the day with the sun
held still (MOPPE_DAY=0); the rest are the autopilots and scripted walks.
Over them runs a quiet HUD drawn as SVG (rsvg-convert, in the bundled
Geomini): a card for each chapter, and for each view its name, what it is,
and where it lies, as latitude and longitude at 60 degrees north (north is
-Z) and metres above the sea.

The clips are kept in DIR (build/vista) and only missing ones are recorded,
so a change to the cut (FILM) or the HUD takes a few minutes; --fresh
records them all again, --only some of them.  --draft encodes quickly.
"""

